1
00:01:42,985 --> 00:01:45,905
WEIYANG PUBLIC
SECURITY BUREAU NANSHAN BRANCH

2
00:01:45,985 --> 00:01:46,945
Over the past few days, we've checked in

3
00:01:47,025 --> 00:01:48,585
with taxi drivers and tricycle operators
across several districts.

4
00:01:48,665 --> 00:01:50,185
None of them picked up
any students heading to Yuanlongli.

5
00:01:50,265 --> 00:01:51,145
What about your side?

6
00:01:51,225 --> 00:01:52,425
Did you check

7
00:01:52,505 --> 00:01:53,545
the supermarkets and shops
around the school?

8
00:01:55,185 --> 00:01:56,665
We have a lead.

9
00:01:56,745 --> 00:01:57,585
Han Zi'ang finally spoke.

10
00:01:58,425 --> 00:01:59,585
What did he say?

11
00:02:00,265 --> 00:02:01,345
Something like this.

12
00:02:07,465 --> 00:02:08,545
"Charon.

13
00:02:09,545 --> 00:02:10,505
Charon the ferryman

14
00:02:11,265 --> 00:02:12,705
carries souls to Yinyi Village.

15
00:02:12,785 --> 00:02:14,065
Horse.

16
00:02:15,425 --> 00:02:16,745
The Trojan Horse.

17
00:02:17,385 --> 00:02:18,265
It eats people.

18
00:02:20,345 --> 00:02:21,545
It's going to eat you."

19
00:02:22,185 --> 00:02:23,065
What are you on about?

20
00:02:24,065 --> 00:02:25,905
He's not fully recovered yet.

21
00:02:25,985 --> 00:02:27,465
He's rambling about anime stuff.

22
00:02:27,545 --> 00:02:29,945
-Nonsense?
-Not exactly.

23
00:02:30,905 --> 00:02:31,745
Explain that.

24
00:02:32,465 --> 00:02:34,905
I can't quite piece it together yet,

25
00:02:34,985 --> 00:02:36,625
but I think what he said

26
00:02:36,705 --> 00:02:39,345
might be connected
to the real-world crime scene.

27
00:02:39,425 --> 00:02:40,425
We should try to decipher it.

28
00:02:43,745 --> 00:02:45,465
What kind of outfit
is that for a detective?

29
00:02:45,545 --> 00:02:46,705
-I was trying to…
-Enough.

30
00:02:46,785 --> 00:02:48,345
Stick to your job.

31
00:02:48,425 --> 00:02:49,945
Head back to the hospital
and stay with Han Zi'ang.

32
00:02:50,025 --> 00:02:52,505
When he's fully awake, question him again.

33
00:02:52,585 --> 00:02:55,265
Stop jumping to conclusions.
You're throwing us off.

34
00:02:55,345 --> 00:02:56,425
Go on.

35
00:02:57,145 --> 00:02:58,945
We've checked all the shops
around the school

36
00:02:59,025 --> 00:03:00,465
and pulled every camera we could find.

37
00:03:00,545 --> 00:03:02,465
Still, nothing unusual turned up.

38
00:03:11,065 --> 00:03:13,545
WHAT DOES TROJAN HORSE MEAN?

39
00:03:13,625 --> 00:03:16,145
If Qu Dahai could make sense of that,

40
00:03:16,225 --> 00:03:18,225
he wouldn't be on this Earth anymore.

41
00:03:19,265 --> 00:03:21,305
It's not entirely his fault.

42
00:03:22,345 --> 00:03:24,185
What Han Zi'ang said
isn't easy to figure out.

43
00:03:29,505 --> 00:03:33,385
If this Yinyi Village

44
00:03:34,225 --> 00:03:35,865
refers to Yuanlongli,

45
00:03:36,785 --> 00:03:38,905
then could Charon the ferryman

46
00:03:39,465 --> 00:03:41,585
be some kind of transport?

47
00:03:41,665 --> 00:03:44,865
The task force is focusing on vehicles.

48
00:03:44,945 --> 00:03:47,265
Commercial cars and tricycles.

49
00:03:48,105 --> 00:03:49,545
What about ride shares?

50
00:03:49,625 --> 00:03:50,905
What ride shares?

51
00:03:51,705 --> 00:03:54,505
Some shops restock
in the morning and at night.

52
00:03:55,145 --> 00:03:57,305
Drivers pick up extra passengers
along the way.

53
00:03:58,025 --> 00:04:00,065
Unlicensed cars like that are too random

54
00:04:00,145 --> 00:04:01,545
to track down.

55
00:04:03,905 --> 00:04:06,265
These five kids skipped school,

56
00:04:06,785 --> 00:04:08,985
but none of the road cameras caught them.

57
00:04:09,585 --> 00:04:11,225
I think we should check

58
00:04:11,305 --> 00:04:15,065
for construction sites near their school.

59
00:04:15,145 --> 00:04:16,225
If there is,

60
00:04:16,305 --> 00:04:18,184
it could mess with the cameras.

61
00:04:18,865 --> 00:04:20,585
Where's the map? Let me see it.

62
00:04:36,665 --> 00:04:38,545
DANFENG MIDDLE SCHOOL,

63
00:04:38,625 --> 00:04:40,545
WEIYANG NO. 2 MIDDLE SCHOOL
WEIYANG NO. 4 MIDDLE SCHOOL

64
00:04:47,745 --> 00:04:49,505
Focus here.

65
00:04:49,585 --> 00:04:50,945
BINCHUAN DISTRICT

66
00:04:51,025 --> 00:04:54,585
WEIYANG STADIUM, WENZHUANG

67
00:05:21,225 --> 00:05:22,985
JIAJIA GROCERY

68
00:05:37,505 --> 00:05:38,385
Where're my cigarettes?

69
00:05:49,185 --> 00:05:50,305
I dropped a pack on the road.

70
00:05:50,385 --> 00:05:51,705
I'll make it up to you.

71
00:05:52,505 --> 00:05:53,705
It's fine.

72
00:05:54,465 --> 00:05:55,305
Let me introduce myself.

73
00:05:55,385 --> 00:05:57,585
I'm Yuan Ziqiang. What about you?

74
00:05:59,385 --> 00:06:00,225
Here's the thing.

75
00:06:00,305 --> 00:06:03,345
I'm driving
to the provincial capital today

76
00:06:03,425 --> 00:06:05,225
to meet up with some friends
from my hometown.

77
00:06:05,305 --> 00:06:07,585
You've been saying
you want to go to Beijing.

78
00:06:07,665 --> 00:06:09,585
There's a train
from the provincial capital.

79
00:06:09,665 --> 00:06:11,985
Do you want to hitch a ride?

80
00:06:12,065 --> 00:06:13,465
I can drop you off there.

81
00:06:24,625 --> 00:06:25,705
About this tall.

82
00:06:25,785 --> 00:06:28,225
She's wearing a green jacket
and dark jeans.

83
00:06:28,305 --> 00:06:29,305
About this tall.

84
00:06:29,385 --> 00:06:30,505
Have you seen this girl?

85
00:06:30,585 --> 00:06:32,265
About this tall.
She's wearing a green jacket.

86
00:06:32,345 --> 00:06:33,225
No.

87
00:06:33,305 --> 00:06:34,585
-Mister, have you seen this girl?
-Mister,

88
00:06:35,385 --> 00:06:36,465
have you seen this girl?

89
00:06:37,345 --> 00:06:38,665
No.

90
00:06:38,745 --> 00:06:40,225
Alright. Thanks.

91
00:06:41,745 --> 00:06:43,945
-How much?
-Two yuan for half a kilo.

92
00:06:44,025 --> 00:06:45,665
Wrap up these three.

93
00:06:45,745 --> 00:06:47,585
JIAJIA GROCERY

94
00:06:54,585 --> 00:06:55,545
It's hot.

95
00:07:02,385 --> 00:07:03,425
Guys,

96
00:07:03,505 --> 00:07:05,585
we've checked eight stops.

97
00:07:05,665 --> 00:07:06,745
But there's not a single trace.

98
00:07:06,825 --> 00:07:08,825
That little tyke is probably gone.

99
00:07:08,905 --> 00:07:10,665
At this rate,

100
00:07:10,745 --> 00:07:12,025
we'll still be at it by Chinese New Year.

101
00:07:13,825 --> 00:07:15,425
Let's head back

102
00:07:16,185 --> 00:07:17,385
and come up with a new plan.

103
00:07:17,465 --> 00:07:20,145
Captain Ran told us to work the route.
There has to be a reason.

104
00:07:20,225 --> 00:07:21,225
Finish up and keep going.

105
00:07:22,985 --> 00:07:23,945
He's here.

106
00:07:27,745 --> 00:07:28,785
How's it going here?

107
00:07:29,945 --> 00:07:32,105
We've got this covered.
Why don't you get some rest?

108
00:07:32,185 --> 00:07:33,225
-You've been running yourself ragged.
-Here.

109
00:07:33,825 --> 00:07:34,945
Grab a bite.

110
00:07:35,945 --> 00:07:37,865
He Xiaohe is just
as insensible as her dad.

111
00:07:37,945 --> 00:07:39,745
Look at what she's doing to Captain Ran.

112
00:07:40,785 --> 00:07:41,865
Don't say that.

113
00:07:41,945 --> 00:07:43,545
I share the blame
for what happened to her.

114
00:07:43,625 --> 00:07:46,025
If I hadn't pushed Sir
to take on that case,

115
00:07:46,105 --> 00:07:48,345
his family might not have fallen apart.

116
00:07:49,105 --> 00:07:51,065
You keep calling him "Sir".

117
00:07:51,145 --> 00:07:52,425
Does He Yuanhang even deserve that?

118
00:07:56,385 --> 00:07:58,065
JIAJIA GROCERY

119
00:08:02,625 --> 00:08:03,945
JIAJIA GROCERY

120
00:08:09,905 --> 00:08:11,385
Did we check the supermarket?

121
00:08:13,945 --> 00:08:15,945
We just got to this street
and are about to check it out.

122
00:08:18,025 --> 00:08:21,025
<i>"Suddenly, over the stream</i>
<i>We heard a pipa sound</i>

123
00:08:21,665 --> 00:08:24,505
<i>I forgot to go home,</i>
<i>And the guest stood spell-bound"</i>

124
00:08:25,265 --> 00:08:27,305
Pen. Pen.

125
00:08:30,505 --> 00:08:32,545
<i>"Song of a Pipa Player,</i> by Bai Juyi.

126
00:08:33,144 --> 00:08:34,185
In the tenth year of Yuanhe's reign…"

127
00:08:34,264 --> 00:08:35,664
What can I get you, misters?

128
00:08:36,345 --> 00:08:37,505
We're with the Nanshan Branch.

129
00:08:38,305 --> 00:08:39,625
Have you seen this girl?

130
00:08:39,705 --> 00:08:41,225
MISSING PERSONS

131
00:08:45,185 --> 00:08:46,225
Have you seen her?

132
00:08:53,865 --> 00:08:55,145
Go back to your studies.

133
00:09:00,545 --> 00:09:03,545
<i>"Suddenly, over the stream</i>
<i>We heard a pipa sound</i>

134
00:09:03,625 --> 00:09:06,785
<i>I forgot to go home,</i>
<i>and the guest stood spell-bound.</i>

135
00:09:06,865 --> 00:09:09,465
<i>We followed the music to its source,</i>

136
00:09:10,465 --> 00:09:13,145
<i>but heard the pipa stop,</i>
<i>and no music in the air.</i>

137
00:09:13,665 --> 00:09:16,625
<i>We moved our boat towards</i>
<i>the one whence came the strain,</i>

138
00:09:17,785 --> 00:09:20,745
<i>brought back the lamp,</i>
<i>asked for more wine and drank again.</i>

139
00:09:21,265 --> 00:09:24,185
<i>Repeatedly, we called</i>
<i>For the fair player still"</i>

140
00:09:26,265 --> 00:09:27,225
Your son is working hard.

141
00:09:28,785 --> 00:09:30,585
He's in high school,
but his grades aren't great.

142
00:09:30,665 --> 00:09:31,865
So I keep an eye on his studies.

143
00:09:31,945 --> 00:09:33,105
Recite it again.

144
00:09:33,185 --> 00:09:35,065
<i>"Song of a Pipa Player,</i> by Bai Juyi.

145
00:09:35,865 --> 00:09:36,985
In the tenth year of Yuanhe's reign…"

146
00:09:37,065 --> 00:09:39,705
Let's move on to the next shop.

147
00:09:40,225 --> 00:09:41,745
Take care.

148
00:09:52,545 --> 00:09:54,225
Putting on a show is way harder

149
00:09:54,305 --> 00:09:56,105
than gaming.

150
00:09:56,185 --> 00:09:57,665
When that girl gets back with supplies,

151
00:09:57,745 --> 00:09:58,905
I'm going to send her home.

152
00:09:58,985 --> 00:10:01,145
-I'm heading inside to practice.
-Hold on.

153
00:10:01,745 --> 00:10:03,705
Wait till the cops are out of sight.

154
00:10:06,385 --> 00:10:08,345
We haven't checked
a hardware store up ahead,

155
00:10:08,425 --> 00:10:10,265
a barbershop, and a mahjong parlor.

156
00:10:11,545 --> 00:10:13,265
Wait. Stay here.

157
00:10:13,345 --> 00:10:14,385
Wait?

158
00:10:14,465 --> 00:10:15,385
How long?

159
00:10:18,825 --> 00:10:20,945
Five minutes. We'll go back to that shop.

160
00:10:27,745 --> 00:10:29,185
Hurry up. Cover for me.

161
00:10:29,265 --> 00:10:30,265
Come on.

162
00:10:42,865 --> 00:10:44,105
Is he your son too?

163
00:10:50,465 --> 00:10:51,505
You do magic tricks,

164
00:10:51,585 --> 00:10:53,145
and your son changes faces.

165
00:10:54,105 --> 00:10:55,425
Five minutes, and he has lost weight?

166
00:11:00,465 --> 00:11:01,865
Officer, I want to come clean.

167
00:11:02,665 --> 00:11:04,145
I saw that girl.

168
00:11:07,625 --> 00:11:09,265
<i>Everyone, look to your left.</i>

169
00:11:09,345 --> 00:11:12,545
<i>This is the first stop</i>
<i>of our Mount Wu tour.</i>

170
00:11:12,625 --> 00:11:13,825
<i>Seeing flowers in the fog.</i>

171
00:11:13,905 --> 00:11:16,025
<i>If we come back in three or four months,</i>

172
00:11:16,105 --> 00:11:18,305
<i>you'll see flowers in the fog</i>

173
00:11:18,385 --> 00:11:19,945
<i>and fog among the flowers.</i>

174
00:11:20,545 --> 00:11:21,905
<i>The heavier the fog,</i>

175
00:11:21,985 --> 00:11:23,385
<i>the more dangerous it is</i>
<i>to head up to the mountain.</i>

176
00:11:23,465 --> 00:11:26,385
<i>Back on August 24th, 1995,</i>

177
00:11:26,465 --> 00:11:28,465
<i>there was an accident.</i>

178
00:11:28,545 --> 00:11:30,145
<i>So once you reach the resort,</i>

179
00:11:30,225 --> 00:11:33,345
<i>remember this, do not</i>
<i>go up the mountain on your own.</i>

180
00:11:50,225 --> 00:11:52,025
JINGLIAN TEMPLE TUNNEL

181
00:11:52,105 --> 00:11:53,105
ROUTE 15 WEIYANG STADIUM TO WENZHUANG

182
00:12:11,905 --> 00:12:13,785
You're not a trafficker, are you?

183
00:12:14,985 --> 00:12:15,945
Sorry?

184
00:12:16,985 --> 00:12:18,865
You're not a trafficker, are you?

185
00:12:24,105 --> 00:12:25,185
Get off at the next stop.

186
00:12:26,065 --> 00:12:27,025
Find your own way back.

187
00:12:38,505 --> 00:12:40,825
JIAJIA GROCERY

188
00:12:40,905 --> 00:12:42,505
Mangkun, head over to Nanhu Market.

189
00:12:43,145 --> 00:12:44,145
Talk to the vendors.

190
00:12:47,145 --> 00:12:48,145
Find out who she hung out with.

191
00:12:49,065 --> 00:12:49,905
What about the four of them?

192
00:12:52,385 --> 00:12:53,345
IDs.

193
00:12:53,425 --> 00:12:54,625
We…

194
00:12:54,705 --> 00:12:56,105
We don't have IDs.

195
00:12:57,425 --> 00:12:59,185
They're in the cybercafé without IDs?

196
00:12:59,265 --> 00:13:01,545
Officer, this is an illegal cybercafé.

197
00:13:01,625 --> 00:13:03,865
It's not his fault. We're all over 18.

198
00:13:03,945 --> 00:13:06,225
We sold our IDs for money

199
00:13:06,305 --> 00:13:08,065
to pay for our training and competitions.

200
00:13:08,145 --> 00:13:10,345
This is gaming, not a competition.

201
00:13:10,425 --> 00:13:11,505
Qu.

202
00:13:12,385 --> 00:13:14,505
-Do you have surveillance here?
-Yes.

203
00:13:31,505 --> 00:13:33,665
Officer, this is the footage
from the past week.

204
00:13:38,505 --> 00:13:39,465
Officer,

205
00:13:39,545 --> 00:13:41,905
we really did see her passed out
in the alley late at night.

206
00:13:41,985 --> 00:13:44,465
We were afraid she'd freeze,
so we brought her back.

207
00:13:44,545 --> 00:13:46,585
This money-grabber squeezes
money out of us every day.

208
00:13:46,665 --> 00:13:48,625
Even if you break wind here,

209
00:13:48,705 --> 00:13:50,825
she'll chase you down and charge you
an air pollution fee.

210
00:13:50,905 --> 00:13:51,865
Sometimes,

211
00:13:51,945 --> 00:13:54,345
when Xiaohe saw us training hard,

212
00:13:54,425 --> 00:13:56,305
she would chip in
and buy us instant noodles.

213
00:13:56,385 --> 00:13:58,585
Yeah. She's not stingy.

214
00:13:58,665 --> 00:14:00,945
She said she was saving up
to go to Beijing.

215
00:14:01,025 --> 00:14:01,785
Beijing?

216
00:14:01,865 --> 00:14:04,145
-To learn rock music.
-That's right.

217
00:14:04,225 --> 00:14:05,345
Go to Beijing to learn rock music.

218
00:14:06,105 --> 00:14:07,305
When did she say that?

219
00:14:07,825 --> 00:14:10,385
ROUTE 15 WEIYANG STADIUM TO WENZHUANG
DONGLIWA STATION

220
00:14:27,585 --> 00:14:29,225
We'll stay there for the night.

221
00:14:31,265 --> 00:14:33,345
Didn't you say we were leaving today?

222
00:14:33,425 --> 00:14:35,865
My friend said
some of them haven't arrived yet.

223
00:14:35,945 --> 00:14:37,545
We'll head out together tomorrow
once everyone's here.

224
00:14:45,585 --> 00:14:46,905
HAPPY SHOPPING MART

225
00:14:51,185 --> 00:14:54,145
YOUCHENG HOTEL

226
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:15,865
Come on in.

227
00:15:23,425 --> 00:15:24,425
Kid,

228
00:15:25,025 --> 00:15:26,425
you're suspicious of everything.

229
00:15:29,265 --> 00:15:30,105
Take a look at this.

230
00:15:35,145 --> 00:15:36,465
YUAN ZIQIANG'S IDENTITY CARD

231
00:15:39,705 --> 00:15:40,665
I'm not lying, right?

232
00:15:40,745 --> 00:15:41,585
CITIZEN IDENTIFICATION

233
00:15:42,465 --> 00:15:43,945
You can have it if you want.

234
00:15:54,825 --> 00:15:57,105
Captain Ran, look at this.

235
00:15:59,785 --> 00:16:01,745
This is footage from 11:05 a.m.

236
00:16:02,345 --> 00:16:03,225
After this man

237
00:16:03,745 --> 00:16:05,985
gave Xiaohe some money, she headed out

238
00:16:06,065 --> 00:16:07,185
and hasn't come back since.

239
00:16:11,945 --> 00:16:13,185
That guy with the glasses

240
00:16:13,265 --> 00:16:15,025
always had Xiaohe
pick up cigarettes for him.

241
00:16:15,105 --> 00:16:17,225
He never asked for change.
He's really generous.

242
00:16:30,585 --> 00:16:32,945
What do you do for a living?

243
00:16:33,585 --> 00:16:34,905
Construction.

244
00:16:34,985 --> 00:16:38,025
I go back and forth between Weiyang
and the provincial capital very often.

245
00:16:38,105 --> 00:16:39,105
And you?

246
00:16:39,185 --> 00:16:41,425
I noticed you've been staying
at the cybercafé every night.

247
00:16:41,505 --> 00:16:43,065
Doesn't your family check on you?

248
00:16:58,425 --> 00:17:00,425
Alright. Food's almost ready.

249
00:17:05,145 --> 00:17:07,025
Instant noodles again?

250
00:17:07,105 --> 00:17:09,665
I eat that three times a day
at the cybercafé.

251
00:17:10,184 --> 00:17:11,905
It makes me sick just looking at it now.

252
00:17:12,505 --> 00:17:13,505
Mister,

253
00:17:13,585 --> 00:17:16,345
can you buy me a proper meal?

254
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:26,025
Little kid,

255
00:17:26,545 --> 00:17:28,224
you're such a hassle.

256
00:17:37,505 --> 00:17:38,305
Don't wander off.

257
00:17:38,905 --> 00:17:39,945
It's not safe out there.

258
00:17:40,465 --> 00:17:42,345
You might get snatched.

259
